---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('activecampaign')!;
const b = appBySlug('sendlane')!;
const path = '/compare/activecampaign-vs-sendlane';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-sendlane');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-sendlane');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Sendlane still an independent purchase option?",
    "answer": "Privy acquired Sendlane. Sendlane still presents a demo enquiry and login, but these sources do not establish standalone new-account terms. Confirm the offered product and migration path."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does ActiveCampaign capture every added cart?",
    "answer": "No such coverage is established. Its Shopify abandonment data requires the documented checkout stage; demonstrate identification and purchase exits in your store."
  },
  {
    "question": "Who should own a wholesale enquiry?",
    "answer": "Assign a salesperson and record the pause and resume rules for promotional recovery. Demonstrate the task handoff instead of assuming an automatic MOQ detector."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the $44 example prove?",
    "answer": "Only hypothetical gross-profit arithmetic: $14.08 at full price versus $9.24 after an 11% code, before other variable costs. It proves no recovery lift."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link text-sm font-bold">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Compare an ActiveCampaign checkout workflow with a Sendlane enquiry in the context of its acquisition by Privy. Establish the current service and human handoff before comparing automation costs.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{"label": "Evaluate", "tool": "ActiveCampaign", "reason": "Demonstrate checkout email and the handoff to your sales team."}, {"label": "Evaluate", "tool": "Sendlane / Privy", "reason": "Confirm the platform, onboarding terms and migration responsibilities being offered today."}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>{a.name}</th><th>{b.name}</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Current scope</td><td>Shopify integration and abandoned-cart email automation.</td><td>Privy acquired Sendlane; confirm which product a new contract supplies.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Queue decision</td><td>Separate automated recovery from open sales enquiries.</td><td>Identify who migrates and owns existing recovery queues.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cost comparison</td><td>Quote the required automation, audience and any sales tooling.</td><td>Obtain current platform, send-volume and migration terms.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Start with the current purchase option</h2>
<p>Privy’s <a href="https://www.privy.com/blog/privy-acquires-sendlane">February 2, 2026 announcement</a> confirms its acquisition of Sendlane. The <a href="https://www.privy.com/sendlane-acquisition">acquisition page</a> describes email, SMS and onsite marketing. The <a href="https://www.sendlane.com/">Sendlane website</a> still presents a demo enquiry and account login. Checked November 25, 2026. These pages do not establish whether a new merchant receives a standalone Sendlane account or a Privy onboarding path. Ask for the current product, contracting entity, feature scope and support responsibilities in writing; neither retirement nor unchanged standalone availability is established here.</p>
<h2>Prove checkout capture before a sales handoff</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001045964-Abandoned-cart-overview">ActiveCampaign documents</a> a Shopify integration, an abandonment trigger and an email cart block. Its Shopify data requires the shopper to reach the documented checkout stage; a product added anonymously to a cart is not equivalent. In a proposed acceptance exercise, compare an anonymous add, an identified checkout and a purchase while a reminder waits. Save event timestamps and the actual recovery destination. Ask the Sendlane/Privy onboarding team to demonstrate the same cases in the product being quoted.</p>
<h2>Handle a minimum-order enquiry as a separate job</h2>
<p>For a wholesale basket below the minimum order quantity, assign a salesperson to explain pack sizes or prepare a quote. Specify what creates the task, who receives the customer and cart identifiers, and what pauses promotional reminders while the enquiry is open. Do not assume either platform automatically detects an MOQ objection. Require a demonstrated field or explicit operator action. Close the task on purchase or a resolved enquiry without replaying the original discount sequence.</p>
<h2>Agree the migration and approval contract</h2>
<p>An existing Sendlane merchant should inventory active flows, waiting messages, sender domains, consent records, coupons and retained reports before changing service. Have the provider state which records and templates transfer and which must be rebuilt. A new merchant should request the same implementation checklist. Name the person who approves copy and incentives, the person who enables sends, and the rollback owner. Reconcile waiting messages before the replacement is activated; a fixed two-week overlap is not an acceptance criterion.</p>
<h2>Rehearse the cart objections</h2>
<p>For financing or BNPL interruption, offer a route to payment help without promising credit approval. For shipping-quote shock, show the applicable destination and shipping terms before offering a code. For a gift message or subscription toggle, follow the recovery link and check the intended purchase details survive. For an unavailable size or bundle coupon, recheck stock and Shopify discount combinations. These exercises distinguish missing checkout context from price resistance; they are not observed recovery results.</p>
<h2>Keep the small-cart arithmetic honest</h2>
<p>Illustrative only: a $44 basket at 32% gross margin has $29.92 goods cost and $14.08 full-price gross profit. An 11% code removes $4.84, leaving $39.16 revenue and $9.24 gross profit. Goods cost stays fixed. Subtract payment, shipping, messaging and returns before calling the remainder contribution. This is not an incentive recommendation or a measured platform outcome.</p>
<h2>Choose from demonstrated operating requirements</h2>
<p>Compare quotes at the same audience, email volume, SMS destinations and support scope, including migration and operator time. Choose ActiveCampaign if the demonstrated checkout and sales workflow meets your needs; choose the offered Sendlane/Privy path if its actual onboarding, queues and service terms do. For a split stack, assign one sender per stage and channel, deduplicate by cart/customer/action and recheck purchase, permission and stock before release. Measure deduplicated orders and contribution; any randomized holdout needs a size and window justified by traffic rather than a universal percentage.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</div></section></BaseLayout>
